        "value": "An illegible mark in solid black type-ink standing in the gutter immediately to the right of the 少參事 count 五人 — the same interlinear slot the confirmed 二人 correction occupies beside the acting-senior-councillor count. It is two pieces: a wedge that is 30px wide at the top and tapers to a point (x723-751, y1433-1450) and a separate dot below it (x733-747, y1469-1479). At 14x the pair forms no readable character; the wedge is wide at the top and narrow at the bottom, which rules out 六 (whose top run widens downward into the lid) and its stroke morphology rules out 二 and 一. Darkness measurement puts it at the same ink density as the main type (min grey 20-24 against paper at 199-215), so it is neither bleed-through nor a paper flaw, and at roughly 414 ink pixels it is far larger than the specks on this page (the next largest residual is 18px). It is recorded rather than transcribed because the 少參事 name-block carries six names against the printed five, which a correction in this position would resolve — but the glyph cannot be read, so no value is assigned. Precedent for boxing a marginal correction on an officials page: the bare 三 on kajiyama_lower_p173_right."
